for $x \in [\varepsilon,1]$. Since $n \neq 1$, $f^{(n)}$ is smooth on all of $[0,1]$, and thus $\Xi^{m,n}_{\varepsilon}$ is smooth as well. Moreover $\lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \Xi^{m,n}_{\varepsilon}(1)=I^A(m,n;\tau)$, due to the periodicity of $f^{(n)}$ (Corollary \ref{cor:fk}). Now
